 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\nThe response contains the payment terms (name and code) for the specified contract account.\n\nError Handling\n\nTypical errors that may occur with this operation are:\n\ne Nocontract account ID is specified in the query\n\ne Thecontract account ID specified in the query is invalid\n\nMessage Types\n\ne ContractAccountPaymentTermsBylDQuery\n\ne\u00a2 ContractAccountPaymentTermsBylDResponse\n\nPrerequisites\n\nThe user has to have the required authorization to read the specified contract account.\n\nNotes on SAP Implementation\nPrerequisites\nYou are using software component FI-CA (as of version FI-CA 6.02).\n\nYou have maintained the backend configuration of SAP Biller Direct in FI-CA (see Customizing for Contract Accounts Receivable\nand Payable under Integration -> Financial Supply Chain Management -> Biller Direct -> Basic Setting for Customer Portal in\n\nInternet ). Note that since this operation is based on the functions of SAP Biller Direct , its use is subject to the same license\nconditions.\n\nThe user has sufficient authorizations, in particular with regard to authorization object F_LKK_EBPP.\n\nProcessing\n\nIf an external contract account ID is specified in the query, it has to be mapped to the corresponding internal contract account ID.\nThis mapping is carried out based on the definition of event 6600.\n\nPayment Behaviour Summary In\n\nDefinition\n\nThe Payment Behaviour In inbound service interface contains an operation that queries payment behavior.\n\nTechnical Data\n\nEntity Type               Service Interface\n",
